## 1. Introduction

An Individual Case Safety Report (ICSR) is a structured document used to report and assess a suspected adverse event associated with a medicinal product. It contains relevant information about the patient, suspected medicine, adverse reaction, clinical history, causality, seriousness, expectedness, management, and outcome.

ICSR processing is an important activity in pharmacovigilance because it supports the identification, evaluation, and monitoring of potential medicine-related safety risks.

This report simulates the work of a Drug Safety Associate by applying standard pharmacovigilance assessment principles to a suspected amoxicillin-associated skin rash.

