### Clinical description

A 45-year-old female developed a skin rash three days after initiating amoxicillin therapy. The suspected medicine was discontinued, following which the patient recovered.

The temporal relationship and improvement after withdrawal support a possible causal association between amoxicillin and the skin rash. However, the absence of detailed clinical findings, allergy history, concomitant medication information, and alternative-cause assessment limits the certainty of the evaluation.

The reaction should be documented as a suspected adverse drug reaction rather than a definitively proven drug-induced event.

