## 19. Conclusion

This educational ICSR evaluates a suspected amoxicillin-associated skin rash in a 45-year-old female patient. The reaction developed three days after treatment initiation, and the patient recovered after the suspected medicine was discontinued.

Based on the available information, the reaction is provisionally classified as **probable/likely according to the WHO-UMC causality approach, non-serious, and expected**. Its severity cannot be reliably graded because the intensity and clinical characteristics of the rash were not documented.

The case demonstrates the importance of structured adverse drug reaction identification, causality assessment, seriousness and expectedness classification, outcome documentation, and follow-up. Additional patient, reporter, and clinical information would be required before considering the case complete for formal regulatory reporting.
